### Outside the diff

- 🟡⚡ **Consider · perf: Removing the deferral makes remote chats poll the file list every 30 s without any "@" (confidence medium)** (`frontend/src/renderer/hooks/useConversation.ts:2256`): `useWorkspaceFilePaths` was gated on `fileMenuAsked`. It is now enabled whenever a snapshot exists (SessionChatSurface.tsx:435). For remote hosts, `refetchInterval` returns 30 s unless the workspace is missing (line 2256), so every open remote chat re-reads the whole list twice a minute, whether or not the user ever types "@". On a daemon without the paths route, that read is the slow `/workspace/files` fallback. The PR body says the list is needed for transcript links, but it doesn't mention the polling. Consider polling only while the composer has asked for the menu, or lengthening the interval.

### Summary

The change is small and mostly correct. I left three "consider" findings and no blockers. The ROUTE_NOT_FOUND memo is module-level and never cleared, so a host whose daemon is upgraded stays on the slow fallback until the app reloads. Dropping the lazy "@" gate now makes remote chats poll the file list every 30 s without any "@" typed. The new test also depends on module state shared between tests. I only read the code and ran nothing.

